 Also called: Hash Grid for Voxel World, HashSet of IVec3
 ## Overview
-The Voxel World Data Structure is a sparse representation for voxel worlds that stores the existence of voxels using a hash set of integer-based 3D vectors. It solves the problem of efficiently tracking which grid-aligned positions contain solid geometry without allocating memory for empty space. It differs from its parent [Hash Grids](936-hash-grids.md) by focusing on discrete world coordinates for voxel placement rather than hashing continuous vertex positions for feature extraction, and it serves as the foundational sparse storage layer for [Multi-type Voxel Storage](1104-multi-type-voxel-storage.md).
